# Estia LangGraph agent — environment template.
# Copy to a `.env` at the REPO ROOT (langgraph.json points "env" there).
# NEVER commit real keys. .env is gitignored.

# ─── Required: model ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anthropic API key for claude-haiku-4-5 (used by ChatAnthropic).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ─── Required: Estia backend (where the tools call back to) ──────────
# Base URL of the Estia backend that exposes /api/internal/agent-tool.
# e.g. https://estia.co.il  (no trailing slash, no /api suffix)
ESTIA_API_BASE=

# ─── Auth: short-lived per-agent signed token (NO static token) ──────
# There is NO shared service token. Each graph RUN is authorized by a
# short-lived (5 min) per-agent token that the caller mints from Estia
# (GET /api/ai/agent-token) and passes via the run config:
#     config: { configurable: { estiaToken: "<token>" } }
# The graph forwards it as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; the backend
# verifies it and derives the agentId from the token claim.
#
# ESTIA_INTERNAL_TOKEN is REMOVED — the static-token model is gone.
# Nothing to set here; the token is per-run, not an env var.

# ─── Optional: LangSmith tracing (auto-wired when set) ───────────────
# LANGSMITH_TRACING=true
# LANGSMITH_API_KEY=
# LANGSMITH_PROJECT=estia-agent
# LANGSMITH_ENDPOINT=https://api.smith.langchain.com
